---
import StaticPage from '../layouts/StaticPage.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
---

<StaticPage path="/accessibility/" h1="Accessibility statement" updated="2026-11-23">
  <p class="mt-6">
    Opus Calculator aims to be usable by everyone, including people who use screen readers, keyboards, voice control or magnification. Our target is
    {SITE.accessibilityTarget} (the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines, version 2.2, level AA).
  </p>

  <h2>What we do</h2>
  <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
    <li>Every field has a visible label, and every error message is tied to the field it belongs to.</li>
    <li>
      Fields, buttons and links can be used with a keyboard, with a visible focus outline, and a link at the top of each page skips straight to the calculator.
    </li>
    <li>Text has enough contrast against its background in both the light and the dark theme, and the colours are checked by automatic tests.</li>
    <li>When a result changes it is announced politely to screen readers once you stop typing, not on every key press.</li>
    <li>Pages are built from plain, structured HTML: one main heading, ordered sections, and descriptive link text.</li>
    <li>
      Pages reflow at 320 pixels wide and when zoomed to 200%, without sideways scrolling. Wide tables scroll inside their own box, which can be reached with
      the keyboard.
    </li>
    <li>The default answer is in the page itself, so it does not depend on scripts to be read.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How it is checked</h2>
  <p>
    Our goal is to run automated accessibility checks (axe-core) against representative pages on every release, and to fix any violation they find. Automated
    checks find only part of the possible problems, so they do not replace testing with people who use assistive technology.
  </p>

  <h2>Known limitations</h2>
  <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
    <li>
      The site has not yet had an audit by an independent accessibility specialist, and has not been tested with every screen reader and browser combination.
    </li>
    <li>
      Some formulas are typeset with mathematical markup. Screen readers vary in how well they read them, so each formula is also written out in words on the
      page.
    </li>
    <li>Date fields use your browser's own date control, which differs between browsers and devices.</li>
    <li>
      The advertisement is supplied by a third party, so we cannot guarantee that its content is accessible. It is always separate from the calculator and never
      needs to be used.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Report a barrier</h2>
  <p>
    If something on the site is hard or impossible for you to use, please write to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email.accessibility}`}>{SITE.email.accessibility}</a>{' '}
    with the page address, what you were trying to do, and the browser and assistive technology you use. We reply within {SITE.respondWithinBusinessDays}{' '}
    business days and tell you what we will do about it.
  </p>
</StaticPage>
